Attribution and provenance of the code in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------

1. Ogg demuxer (miniopus.c, "ogg demuxer" section)

   A C translation of micro-ogg-demuxer's OggDemuxer class.

   micro-ogg-demuxer
   Copyright 2025 Kevin Ahrendt
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   https://github.com/esphome-libs/micro-ogg-demuxer
   (an esphome-libs / Open Home Foundation project)

   The port keeps the original's states, functions and result codes
   (EXPECT_HEADER / ACCUM_HEADER / PROCESS_SEGMENTS, zero-copy packet return,
   bounded assembly buffer with oversized-packet skipping, streaming raw-body
   mode, BOS/serial/page-sequence/continuation/EOS validation, resetForSeek and
   the mode-switch guard), so the two sources can be read side by side. The
   result codes are micro-ogg's numeric values unchanged; their names carry
   MiniOpus's MOGG_RES_ prefix where micro-ogg writes OGG_.

2. Ogg page access, granule bisection, seek chain (miniopus.c, "page-level
   reads", "granule math", "granule bisection", "seek" sections) and the
   streaming Vorbis-comment parser

   Ported from UMP-STMH7, an STM32H7 music player by the same author as MiniOpus:
   App/audio/decoders/opus/{opus.c, ogg_pages.{h,c}, ogg_shim.{h,cpp},
   opus_meta.{h,c}}. Those files are the author's own work; the author licenses
   them here under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and that grant covers
   everyone - including the author's previous PolyForm-licensed copies.

   UMP-STMH7
   Copyright 2026 Luigi Pizzolito

   The engineering lessons recorded in UMP-STMH7's change notes (C1, C6, C24,
   C27) are the reason several behaviours here look fussy: pre-skip trimmed in
   float units, a decode scratch sized for two channels of one 60 ms packet, a
   header-slice budget that fails an open instead of falling through mid-packet,
   page-granule hops over granule -1 pages, and a comment header parsed from
   declared lengths without ever reading the album art. Each is commented where
   it appears.

